Where the Minister of Patriots and Veterans Affairs re-determines the disability rating of a person who has rendered distinguished service to the State who has obtained the determination of a disability rating on the physical examination (including a june 18 wounded freedom seeker and a civilian military employee engaged in battle; hereinafter the same shall apply) under the former provisions as at the time this Act enters into force, and a person referred to in the former Article 73-2, he or she shall conduct a physical examination for re-determination under the amended provisions of Article 6-3(2)4 and determine a disability rating.
Article 3 (Applicability to payment of veterans' benefits concerning physical examination for re-determination)
(1) For a person of national merit who has undergone a physical examination for re-determination under the amended provision of Article 6-3(2)4 of pursuant to Article 2 of the Addenda since July 1, 2012, and a person who falls under the former (before July 1, 2012; hereafter the same shall apply in this Article) Article 73-2 (including a person who is deemed to have dismissed the application for physical examination due to no change in the grade of injury as a result of the physical examination for re-determination pursuant to the amended provisions of Article 6-3(3)2) and his or her bereaved family or family, Veterans benefits under the amended provisions of Article 11 at the time of July 1, 2012 (including the amended provisions of the presidential decree on allowances under paragraph (2)7 of the same Article; hereinafter the same shall apply) shall be paid according to the relevant grade of injury.
(2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), veterans benefits shall be paid in accordance with the previous regulations if the monthly total amount of veterans benefits to be paid according to the results of the physical examination for re-determination under paragraph (1) is less than the monthly total amount of veterans benefits paid under the previous regulations.
(3) Where a person of national merit who has undergone a physical examination pursuant to the previous regulations and has been judged to be of a different grade or a person falling under Article 73-2 does not undergo a physical examination for re-determination under Article 6-3(2)4 after July 1, 2012, notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 11, the former provisions shall apply to the payment of veterans benefits to the relevant national meritorious persons and persons falling under Article 73-2 and their bereaved families or families.
